<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sătīcŭla</span></b> ,
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Samnium</i>, <i>on the
				frontiers of Campania</i>, now <i>S. Agata dei
				Goti</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 7, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">23, 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1,
				14, 4</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sătīcŭlānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Saticula</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					23, 14</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.—Plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sătīcŭlā-ni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Saticula</i>, <i>the
				Saticulans</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sătīcŭ-lus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a Saticulan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">asper (collectively),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 729</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
